start('From question to research','01 / Your route through the app','A considered workflow, guided by your own judgement.')
for a,b in [('1. Understand','Enter a ticker. Read what the company does and check the source, currencies, fiscal years and data coverage.'),('2. Investigate','Examine quality, cash flow and debt. Open the sections that help answer your research question.'),('3. Value','Explore cash-flow and dividend assumptions in DCF, Gordon Growth and the valuation lab. Model values are not buy recommendations.'),('4. Record','Add the analysis to your research dossier. Write down your thesis, risks and the evidence that would change your mind.'),('5. Explore','Compare companies if useful, or request a paid AI analysis.')]:row(a,b)
heading('In this guide')
para('03 Installation and getting started · 04 Valuation and currencies · 05 Quality and history · 06 Your research dossier · 07 AI interpretation · 08 Accounts and saving · 09 Reports and practical help · 10 The Mac workspace · 11 Transfers',small)
box('An initial screen, not a final verdict','The app organises financial data and makes assumptions visible. A high score does not prove a durable competitive advantage or guarantee a safe investment. Investigate important findings in the company’s annual reports.')

start('Your first analysis','02 / Installation and getting started','For an Apple Silicon Mac running macOS 14 or later.')
heading('Install the complete app')
para('Open the DMG and drag <b>Tickertwister Desktop.app</b> into <b>Applications</b>. Launch it from Applications, then eject the disk image. The Documentatie folder contains the guides, licences and source code.')
para('When installing an update, save your dossier changes and quit the previous version first. macOS may ask you to confirm that you want to open the downloaded app.',small)
heading('Choose your company')
para('Use a Yahoo ticker such as AAPL, MSFT, SONY or ASML.AS. Click <b>Analyse company</b>. An internet connection is needed for fresh market data; a saved analysis can be opened without fetching Yahoo data again.')
heading('Make the workspace yours')
para('Open <b>Preferences</b> at sign-in or in the toolbar after signing in. The first launch uses the macOS language when supported and otherwise starts in English. Choose light, dark or automatic appearance and a green, blue, brown or purple accent.')
heading('Find your way around')
para('Use <b>Command-F</b> to search inside collapsed sections. Press Enter for the next match. Choose <b>Analysis</b> to enter a ticker. Open your <b>Research dossier</b> and expand the company list to select and compare saved companies.')
box('Check your version',f'The app footer displays v{VERSION}. You can also check Tickertwister Desktop > About Tickertwister Desktop. Save your dossier changes and quit the app before installing an update.')

start('Value rests on assumptions','03 / Models and currency','Understand the cash flow before interpreting the price.')
heading('Start with Owner Earnings')
para('Industrial businesses start from net income plus depreciation, less estimated maintenance investment, plus the cash effect of working capital. For payment processors the model excludes settlement flows and deducts total capital expenditure. For banks and insurers it uses net income as an equity cash flow proxy. If the latest observation differs by more than 30% from its three-year average, the model starts from that average.')
heading('Ten years and a terminal value')
para('Each projected cash flow is discounted to today. Year ten’s terminal value is the following year’s cash flow divided by the discount rate less perpetual growth. For banks and insurers, divide the discounted flows by the share count. The model for other businesses first deducts net debt. Sources and assumptions shows the bridge used for the selected company.')
heading('Choose growth and discount rates')
para('Financial companies start with revenue growth, falling back to net income and then Owner Earnings growth. Operating businesses average available growth rates across the same periods and use net income growth when cash flow growth diverges sharply. The range has a −20% floor and 10% and 12% caps. Perpetual growth starts at 2%.')
para('For banks and insurers you can enter your own cost of equity. Payment companies start with the available WACC. For operating companies the minimum is 6% or the ten-year yield in the cash-flow currency, whichever is higher. Restore initial values reapplies the model assumptions.')
heading('Gordon Growth: an optional dividend perspective')
para('For a stable dividend policy, enter the annual dividend per share D0. The model calculates next year’s dividend as D1 = D0 × (1 + g) and value as D1 / (r − g). Check the source and currency of D0. Retained earnings and share buybacks can help explain a difference from the DCF estimate.')
para('The projection and sensitivity tables use the full section width. Changing an assumption updates the model and its range.')


start('Look behind the score','04 / Quality and financial history','The score helps frame questions. The underlying figures provide context.')
heading('39 criteria with visible scoring')
para('Open Score criteria to see each formula, result and annual values. A criterion may contain several base and trend rules. Missing criteria are not scored as zero; they are excluded from the available scoring weight. Always consider data coverage alongside the score.')
heading('Adjust the weights')
para('Open <b>My weighting</b>. Use the search field and compact editor to find a criterion. A factor of 1 retains the original weight, 2 doubles its importance and 0 excludes it. The scoring rules within each criterion stay the same. Restore original weighting resets the factors.')
box('Your personal score','For a failed or partially met criterion, tick the override to award its available points in your personal score. Clear it to restore the calculated score. The original result and source figures remain available. The analysis saves your overrides and weights.')
heading('Most recent figures first')
para('Open each score criterion for its scoring rules and annual table. Additional series without a score appear in the same section. Dates run from newest on the left to oldest on the right. A dash indicates missing or unusable data. Read the unit above each table.')
heading('Quality checks and annual reports')
para('Orange means investigate, green means no signal under that rule, and grey means not assessable. These are rules of thumb, not sector-specific standards. Banks, insurers, exceptional profits and major acquisitions need additional interpretation.')

start('Your private research dossier','05 / From analysis to conviction','A separate workspace, with no model analysis underneath.')
heading('Open, close and return')
para('Save a company from its ticker analysis to the research dossier. In <b>My companies</b>, choose <b>View analysis</b> to reopen it or expand the list to select another company.')
row('My companies','Search by name, ticker or status. Click a name for its notes. Compare selects companies for study and printing. Export selects companies for transfer. These selections are independent.')
row('Financial research data','Select an available common period or maximum history. The app states the actual dates and method. Long-term comparisons can use fiscal year-ends up to 190 days apart; check the context.')
row('My investment thesis','Four resizable text fields appear in two columns. Record your arguments, risks, counter-evidence and next question. The review date can include an optional hour and minute. Status colours: grey Researching, orange Watch, red Too hard and green Investment candidate.')
row('Interpretation','Open the AI controls in the research dossier. The AI result appears across the full width.')
para('<b>Removing companies.</b> Click × next to a company and confirm Remove. Repeat for each company, then click Save dossier changes once. Until then, Undo removal restores companies and their notes one at a time, most recent first. Each restored company returns to its original position. The AI archive and standalone analysis files are kept separately.',small)

start('AI by deliberate choice','06 / Interpretation and conclusion','Each AI analysis requires your consent to a paid OpenAI API request.')
row('Analysis profile','Luna is the default for lower-cost screening. Sol and Astra offer more demanding analysis profiles at higher cost. There is no automatic model switch or paid retry.')
row('Reasoning effort','Choose Low, Medium or High. Medium is the starting setting. Higher effort can require more tokens and time.')
row('Token limit','8192 is the default limit for reasoning and the answer combined. The requested report remains around 350-500 words in seven sections. The limit does not guarantee a complete answer.')
row('Output language','AI initially follows the app language. Select any of the seven languages independently if preferred. The choice is remembered. Existing results remain available in their original language; a requested API translation is a separate paid action.')
heading('Review, consent and request')
para('Open the Disclaimer and, if useful, inspect the exact financial input. Tick consent to transmission and costs, then click <b>Generate AI interpretation and conclusion</b>. Opening the panel alone costs nothing. Enter your OpenAI API key in the secure Mac dialog. Keys from other providers are not supported. A− and A+ resize the complete AI text; saved AI analyses also have reading-size controls.')
para('Input includes financial data, criteria, weights and quality scores. Your own valuation assumptions and personal notes are not sent. The result and its financial input are automatically archived locally, independently of manually saving your thesis.',small)
box('Treat the opinion as research, not fact','Check AI statements against source documents. Reject, wait, too hard and investment candidate are conclusions for further screening, not guarantees or personal investment advice. API translation is optional, paid and preserves the original.')

start('Work privately and save','07 / Accounts and data','Local accounts separate dossiers. Reliable backups still matter.')
heading('Your own account')
para('Create a local account at sign-in. In account management you can change your name or password. Removing a profile deletes its local data after confirmation. Back up the data you want to keep first.')
para('Use a password manager. There is <b>no password recovery</b>. Sign in again after quitting. Use Lock / switch user before someone else uses the Mac; there is no automatic inactivity lock.')
heading('Remember your API key')
para('With a local account, you can select Save in macOS Keychain in the native key dialog. The key is additionally encrypted with your profile vault. Otherwise it remains only in native memory for the session. Forget API key removes it from memory and Keychain.')
heading('Three different ways to save')
row('Save analysis','An unencrypted .tickertwister file contains figures, assumptions and the ticker’s Quick notes. Open analysis restores the snapshot offline.')
row('Save changes','Writes your dossier and personal notes to disk. A save button also appears near the text fields. An unsaved company removal can still be undone.')
row('AI archive','AI analyses are saved automatically. Select individual analyses to print or remove one after confirmation.')
para('A local account encrypts its dossier and AI archive. A .ttdossier transfer has its own password. PDFs, the general market cache and old backups fall outside the profile encryption. Back up ~/Library/Application Support/Tickertwister/Profiles and keep your passwords separately.',small)

start('From workspace to report','08 / Printing and practical help','Choose the report that supports your next research step.')
heading('Company report')
para('Click Print report in the model analysis. This report includes the company description, quality score, selected owner-earnings DCF or Gordon Growth valuation, its assumptions, key ratios, charts, checks and available notes.')
heading('Research dossier')
para('Print the active company or checked companies from the dossier. Selected companies are printed; with no checkboxes selected, the active company is used. Current notes are included even before saving. Under Saved AI analyses, select the AI texts to append. Without a selection, no AI appendices are printed.')
heading('Missing data or something not working?')
row('No fresh data','Check the ticker and internet connection. Yahoo may limit requests; try again later. A saved analysis does not refresh itself.')
row('Blank margin or dividend','Check whether comparable prices, dividends and share counts are available. Different currencies require a confirmed exchange rate and compatible share data.')
row('Incomplete AI answer','API costs may already have been incurred. There is no automatic retry. Check the settings and increase the token limit only if you choose to request again.')
heading('Sources, rights and limits')
para('Financial data: Yahoo Finance via yfinance 1.8.0. Calculation rules: Tickertwister / FinAnalysis, inspired by the work of Mary Buffett and David Clark. App code is supplied under AGPLv3; see LICENSE and NOTICE for the precise terms and third-party components. Data licences are separate from the code licence. The illustration was generated for this project.',small)
para('Sony ADR ratio: official Sony announcement filed with the SEC, 14 May 2024. The app retains the source with the share basis. AI pricing: developers.openai.com/api/docs/pricing. Translation review by native financial specialists is pending. Documentation reviewed: 27 November 2026.',small)
